\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {S1}{\ignorespaces E2 path restoration and timely service answer different questions. (a--c) Bars show on-time and late completion percentages over all 320 runs per site and policy. The separate counts below give restored/actually affected primary air chains for B1/B2/B4b. Recovery denominators can depend on prior policy actions; B0 has no affected-air-chain denominator. Blue and orange encode deadline outcome here, not policy identity. Table S2 retains the full summaries and exact restoration counts.}}{11}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{sfig:e2}{{S1}{11}{E2 path restoration and timely service answer different questions. (a--c) Bars show on-time and late completion percentages over all 320 runs per site and policy. The separate counts below give restored/actually affected primary air chains for B1/B2/B4b. Recovery denominators can depend on prior policy actions; B0 has no affected-air-chain denominator. Blue and orange encode deadline outcome here, not policy identity. Table S2 retains the full summaries and exact restoration counts}{figure.1}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {S2}{\ignorespaces E4B D60 command sequences after identical-command deduplication. The pending air dispatch is superseded by a ground-fallback decision at the fault time. Ground executes at 420 s and completes at 602 s, after the 480 s deadline. Orange denotes the air command, blue the ground service and red the fault/deadline. Dashed lines denote pending commands and solid lines actual transport. Corrected B0 ground service executes at 360 s and completes at 542 s; B4b changes mode and completes at 602 s.}}{12}{figure.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{sfig:queue}{{S2}{12}{E4B D60 command sequences after identical-command deduplication. The pending air dispatch is superseded by a ground-fallback decision at the fault time. Ground executes at 420 s and completes at 602 s, after the 480 s deadline. Orange denotes the air command, blue the ground service and red the fault/deadline. Dashed lines denote pending commands and solid lines actual transport. Corrected B0 ground service executes at 360 s and completes at 542 s; B4b changes mode and completes at 602 s}{figure.2}{}}
